  "text_pages": [
    "Borrowing - Ordering | ZHAW University Library\nSearch for\nDelete search term\nSearch\nBorrowing - Ordering\nFind out more about borrowing, ordering, collecting, renewing and returning items within the extensive swisscovery network.\nLoans\nCollection\nRenewals\nReturns\n«Thanks to the library's well-networked and interconnected operations, those of us in smaller locations can also benefit from its full range of services.»\nDr. Lukas Neutsch\n, lecturer\nLibrary customers must have a SWITCH edu-ID account to use the swisscovery services.\nRegister for swisscovery\nPlease note:\nIf you do not yet have a SWITCH edu-ID account, you can create one during registration.\nWe recommend that you enter the barcode of your current library ID card. If you do not have a library card yet, you can get one at the information desk of your library.\nZHAW members must have linked their SWITCH edu-ID account to their university affiliation in order to take full advantage of the services of the ZHAW University Library. As a ZHAW member, you will find instructions for creating and linking the edu-ID in the\nSelf-Service-Portal\n(with ZHAW login).\nFor help with the registration, please see the\nSLSP Help Page\n.\nAfter you register with SLSP, you can use your SWITCH edu-ID account for all SLSP libraries.\nLogin to ZHAW swisscovery\nFrequently asked questions\nUniversity Library terms of use\nBy using the University Library, you accept the terms of use.\nUniversity Library terms of use\nThe majority of the items in the ZHAW holding are freely accessible and, with the exception of the non-circulating items (Präsenzbestand), borrowable.\nWith SLSP courier it is possible for you to have books delivered from one library to another within three working days for a fee of CHF 6 - 8 per ordered document. These fees are waived for ZHAW staff and students with appropriate proof.\nYou can find out which libraries are participating in SLSP courier during the ordering process.\nZHAW swisscovery\nFAQ - Frequently Asked Questions about swisscovery\nFound nothing in ZHAW swisscovery?\nIn addition to print media, the University Library has licensed a large holding of electronic media. Please note that if you wish to use e-media off campus, you must connect to the ZHAW network via VPN.\nElectronic media: search - find\nHow to use electronic media\nAs soon as the items you have requested have arrived at your collection location, you will be notified by email.\nCollect media in...\nWinterthur: Information desk\nZurich: Delivery area\nWädenswil: Information desk\nYou can have your media collected by third parties at all locations of the University Library. For a one-time authorisation, send the collection invitation with details of the person collecting to the respective location (\ncontact information at the bottom of this page\n).\nAs a ZHAW staff member, you can have your media collected regularly by a defined third party. To do so, issue the following collection authorisation.\nZHAW staff: power of proxy for arrange collection of media by a third party (in German) (PDF 9.31 kB)\nLoan periods can vary depending on the type of resource and the library it is held by.\nThe standard loan period is 28 days. The documents are automatically renewed up to 5 times in the user account. On condition that they have not been reserved by another person.\nForgotten your password?\nReset your password for swisscovery on the\nSWITCH edu-ID page\n.\nIf you are a ZHAW member, please contact the\nServiceDesk\nfor problems with your ZHAW login.\nReturn media to the library where you picked it up. The exception is media obtained through the SLSP Courier, these can be returned to any library that participates in the SLSP Courier.\nTo return an item outside opening hours, go to your\nhome library\n(Winterthur, Zurich or Wädenswil). Please note that late returns may incur a\nfee\n.\nOur locations\nUniversity Library Winterthur\nVisit us at our Winterthur location in the Sulzer-Areal.\nUniversity Library Winterthur\nUniversity Library Zurich\nVisit us at our Zurich location in the Toni Areal.\nUniversity Library Zurich\nUniversity Library Wädenswil\nVisit us at our location in Wädenswil.\nUniversity Library Wädenswil\nUniversity Library Winterthur\nUniversity Library Zurich\nUniversity Library Wädenswil\nVisit us at our Winterthur location in the Sulzer-Areal.\nVisit us at our Zurich location in the Toni Areal.\nVisit us at our location in Wädenswil.\nUniversity Library Winterthur\nUniversity Library Zurich\nUniversity Library Wädenswil"
  ],
